IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-nouns`

-- g2-fixtures.l4: ready-made case values for the tests of group G2 (and for anyone who wants to call its exports): purposes, the facts that Article 6 reads about a purpose, entities,
-- constitutions, and determinations of public benefit.  Data only: no rules, no directives.
-- A record is built positionally (OF) only where its fields are inherently a row, and then a ruler comment names the columns once.

§ `Fixtures for the tests of Articles 3 to 7`

§§ `Purposes`

-- A purpose recorded under a head, with no flag set.
GIVEN head IS A `Head of charitable purpose`
GIVETH A Purpose
`a G2 purpose recorded under` head MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS "a purpose recorded under a head"
               , head IS JUST head
               , `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

-- A purpose with no head and no flag set: it falls under none of the heads.
GIVETH A Purpose
`a G2 purpose that falls under no head` MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS "a purpose that falls under no head"
               , head IS NOTHING
               , `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

-- A purpose with no head that is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity.
GIVETH A Purpose
`a G2 ancillary purpose` MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS "an ancillary purpose"
               , head IS NOTHING
               , `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS TRUE
               , `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

-- A purpose of advancing a political party or promoting a candidate, with no head.
GIVETH A Purpose
`a G2 political purpose` MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS "a political purpose"
               , head IS NOTHING
               , `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS TRUE
               , `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

-- A political purpose that is also recorded under a head, and one that is also flagged ancillary.
GIVEN head IS A `Head of charitable purpose`
GIVETH A Purpose
`a G2 political purpose recorded under` head MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS "a political purpose recorded under a head"
               , head IS JUST head
               , `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS TRUE
               , `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

GIVETH A Purpose
`a G2 political purpose that is also flagged ancillary` MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS "a political purpose that is also flagged ancillary"
               , head IS NOTHING
               , `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS TRUE
               , `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS TRUE
               , `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

-- A purpose of advancing a philosophical belief, with no head.
GIVETH A Purpose
`a G2 purpose of advancing a philosophical belief` MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS "a purpose of advancing a philosophical belief"
               , head IS NOTHING
               , `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS TRUE

-- A purpose of advancing a philosophical belief that is also recorded under the advancement of religion.
GIVETH A Purpose
`a G2 purpose of advancing a philosophical belief recorded under religion` MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS "a purpose of advancing a philosophical belief recorded under religion"
               , head IS JUST `the advancement of religion`
               , `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE
               , `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS TRUE

§§ `The facts that Article 6 reads about a purpose`

-- Columns: sickness or suffering, regeneration, civic responsibility etc., the sport involves physical skill and exertion, facilities for people in need, facilities open to the public at large,
-- relief by accommodation or care, promotes equality, promotes diversity, the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life (Article 6(1)(i); added after independent testing), the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care (Article 6(2)(e), fork F2.14; the seventh column entails it, so the fixture that sets the seventh sets this one).
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: nothing relevant` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: rural or urban regeneration` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: a sport that involves physical skill and exertion` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: a pastime that involves no physical skill and exertion` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: facilities primarily for people in need` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: facilities open to the public at large` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: facilities neither for people in need nor open to the public at large` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: facilities not for people in need, openness not stated` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, JUST FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: facilities for people in need, with the object of improving the conditions of life` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: facilities open to the public at large, with the object of improving the conditions of life` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: facilities for people in need, without the object of improving the conditions of life` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST FALSE, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: facilities open to the public at large, without the object of improving the conditions of life` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST FALSE, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: the object of improving the conditions of life, facilities neither for people in need nor open to the public at large` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: the object of improving the conditions of life, openness and need not stated` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: without the object of improving the conditions of life, openness and need not stated` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST FALSE, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: relief by the provision of accommodation or care` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE
-- Article 6(2)(e), fork F2.14.  The witness: a purpose of providing accommodation or care with nobody shown to be in need (the seventh column, which carries the need element, is FALSE).
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE
-- The seventh column alone, as a caller that predates the eleventh would write it: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded.
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: equality and diversity both promoted` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, JUST TRUE, JUST TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: diversity promoted, equality not` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: equality promoted, diversity not stated` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, JUST TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: equality not promoted, diversity not stated` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`G2 facts: equality not stated, diversity promoted` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, NOTHING, JUST TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE

-- A purpose together with its facts.
GIVEN p IS A Purpose
      f IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`the G2 purpose` p `with` f MEANS
    `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` OF p, f

GIVEN head IS A `Head of charitable purpose`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`the G2 pair of a purpose with nothing relevant recorded under` head MEANS
    `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` OF (`a G2 purpose recorded under` head), `G2 facts: nothing relevant`

§§ `Entities`

-- Entities whose standing and purposes are given.  Group G2 reads the standing, the purposes and, since the repair of Article 5(1), whether `kinds of entity` is empty (an entity within none of the
-- sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) is not an entity and cannot meet the charity test); every entity below is a company, and a body that is not an entity is built last.  The rest is not read.

GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      ps IS A LIST OF Purpose
GIVETH AN Entity
`a G2 entity with standing` standing `and these G2 purposes` ps MEANS
    Entity WITH name IS "an entity"
              , `standing on the register` IS standing
              , `kinds of entity` IS (LIST `a company`)
              , `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
              , governors IS EMPTY
              , purposes IS ps

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF Purpose
GIVETH AN Entity
`a G2 entity with these purposes` ps MEANS
    Entity WITH name IS "an entity"
              , `standing on the register` IS `not on the register`
              , `kinds of entity` IS (LIST `a company`)
              , `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
              , governors IS EMPTY
              , purposes IS ps

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF Purpose
GIVETH AN Entity
`a G2 applicant with these purposes` ps MEANS
    Entity WITH name IS "an applicant"
              , `standing on the register` IS `an applicant for registration`
              , `kinds of entity` IS (LIST `a company`)
              , `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
              , governors IS EMPTY
              , purposes IS ps

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF Purpose
GIVETH AN Entity
`a G2 registered charity with these purposes` ps MEANS
    Entity WITH name IS "a registered charity"
              , `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
              , `kinds of entity` IS (LIST `a company`)
              , `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
              , governors IS EMPTY
              , purposes IS ps

-- A body that is not an entity: it falls within none of the sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1), for example a partnership, or (on 15 October 2025, before paragraph (ba) was added) an NPO body corporate.
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      ps IS A LIST OF Purpose
GIVETH AN Entity
`a G2 non-entity standing as` standing `holding these G2 purposes` ps MEANS
    Entity WITH name IS "a partnership"
              , `standing on the register` IS standing
              , `kinds of entity` IS EMPTY
              , `is a Jersey entity` IS FALSE
              , governors IS EMPTY
              , purposes IS ps

-- The purposes of an entity, in the form that the charity test takes alongside the entity.
GIVEN pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
GIVETH A LIST OF Purpose
`the G2 purposes in` pfs MEANS
    map (GIVEN pf YIELD pf's purpose) pfs

§§ `Constitutions`

GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`a G2 constitution that expressly permits nothing of the kinds Article 5(2) names` MEANS
    `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` OF EMPTY

GIVEN what IS A `What a constitution expressly permits`
      who IS A `Person named in Article 5(2)`
      capacity IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`a G2 constitution that expressly permits` what `by` who `with the capacity` capacity MEANS
    `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` OF (LIST (`Permission that a constitution expressly makes` OF what, who, capacity))

-- Persons.
GIVETH A `Person named in Article 5(2)`
`a Minister who holds the office of the Chief Minister` MEANS `a Minister` (JUST `the Chief Minister`)
GIVETH A `Person named in Article 5(2)`
`a Minister who holds the office of Minister for External Relations` MEANS `a Minister` (JUST `the Minister for External Relations`)
GIVETH A `Person named in Article 5(2)`
`a Minister who holds another ministerial office, the Minister for Health, say` MEANS `a Minister` NOTHING

§§ `Determinations of public benefit`

-- Columns: who made it; finds the entity provides public benefit; finds the entity intends to provide it; had regard to the guidance; had regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a);
-- benefit goes to a section of the public only; had regard to undue restriction under 7(2)(b); presumed a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit;
-- the entity benefits only identified natural persons; treated identified natural persons as a section of the public.
-- The name of each ends with the maker, so that the maker is the only argument and comes last.

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a proper determination that the entity provides public benefit, made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a proper determination that the entity does not provide public benefit, made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a proper determination that the entity intends to provide public benefit, made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a), made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a determination that provides public benefit for a section of the public without regard to undue restriction, made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a determination that provides public benefit for a section of the public with regard to undue restriction, made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a determination that does not provide public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a determination that treats identified natural persons as a section of the public, made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

GIVEN maker IS A `Legal actor`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the guidance, made by` maker MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` OF maker, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
